Your example shows necessity of adding a term string that spans over the=20
statement to the left. I think it is not very difficult to implement=20
grammatically zo'au-clause: just creating a structure like prenex, and make=
=20
it elidible famyma'o of a statement.=20

However, zo'au-clause will produce more complex semantics than the current=
=20
for the following reason:=20
logical items like negation, numbers and bound variables semantically span=
=20
over the following items, and "postnex" should break the logical structure=
=20
of the leading statement when it appears at the end of the statement.=20

It is not good for me, and I don't intend to implement "postnex" to la=20
zantufa for now.

An alternative idea is to use {no'a} with SEI (or experimental _new_ SOI of=
=20
la ilmentufa):
tu'e lo mabla cu fasnu .i lo zabna cu fasnu tu'u sei ca lo nu mi stuvi'e le=
=20
sralygu'e cu no'a=20


